<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Androclus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Androklos</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Androclus was the legendary founder of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ephesus">Ephesus</a>, said to be a son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/codrus">Codrus of Athens</a> who led Ionian settlers across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a>. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strabo">Strabo</a> and Pausanias, an oracle told him to found a city where a fish and a boar would show him, and he drove out the local <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carians">Carians</a> and Lelegians. He was honoured in Ephesus as founder hero, with a tomb shown to visitors.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/androclus.jpg" alt="Androclus" width="320" height="386" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Briton Rivière · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Briton_Riviere_-_Androcles_and_the_Lion_-_1915-3_-_Auckland_Art_Gallery.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
